WEBVTT

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:05.330
Claude Code and Codex are two of the best coding agents you can run.

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:06.930
They come from different labs.

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:08.290
They think differently.

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:10.700
And they catch different mistakes.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.030
But they can't talk to each other.

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:16.550
So when you want a second opinion, you become the messenger.

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:19.910
Copy. Paste. Copy. Paste.

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:23.440
And something always gets lost in between.

00:00:24.333 --> 00:00:25.643
Meet huddle.

00:00:25.693 --> 00:00:28.803
It lets Claude Code and Codex talk to each other.

00:00:28.853 --> 00:00:30.293
Directly.

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:36.070
Type slash huddle in Claude Code, and dollar huddle in Codex.

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:39.190
That's it. No codes. No IDs.

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:42.750
Each agent is known by its own thread, and they stay connected until

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:44.400
you end it.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:47.130
Now give them something hard.

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:51.940
Retries are double-charging a customer, and nobody knows why.

00:00:52.033 --> 00:00:54.943
Claude proposes a lock around the retry.

00:00:54.993 --> 00:00:59.210
Codex disagrees, and says why, with a file and a line.

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:02.463
The retry fires on jobs that have already committed.

00:01:02.513 --> 00:01:04.223
A lock won't stop that.

00:01:04.273 --> 00:01:06.463
Claude checks, and concedes.

00:01:06.513 --> 00:01:11.033
Together, they land on a better fix than either one found alone.

00:01:12.433 --> 00:01:13.823
That's the point.

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:15.863
They don't just agree with each other.

00:01:15.913 --> 00:01:19.343
They push back with evidence, say when they've been persuaded,

00:01:19.393 --> 00:01:21.983
and close every question with what's agreed,

00:01:22.033 --> 00:01:25.673
what's still open, and who does what next.

00:01:26.567 --> 00:01:28.757
And you stay in charge.

00:01:28.807 --> 00:01:32.837
Run huddle watch in a spare terminal to follow the conversation live.

00:01:32.887 --> 00:01:34.597
Step in whenever you like.

00:01:34.647 --> 00:01:38.837
Your message always comes first, and nothing they decide happens without

00:01:38.887 --> 00:01:40.767
your yes.

00:01:41.767 --> 00:01:43.797
Under the hood, it's simple.

00:01:43.847 --> 00:01:47.317
No server. No account. No telemetry.

00:01:47.367 --> 00:01:51.967
Every message lives in one SQLite file on your machine.

00:01:54.167 --> 00:01:57.317
One command to install. Two agents.

00:01:57.367 --> 00:02:01.727
One conversation. huddle. Let them talk.
